+# Canonical sparse first-action review
+
+Mathematical verdict: PASS for the stated supplied-model, exact-midpoint-family conditional theorem. One narrow supporting-control wording correction is requested below; no mathematical source change or native rerun is needed.
+
+Bound source: SOURCE_FREEZE4635af85ad45365d77419173b1eb25643e34699b694071fa11a7f453aab69f55; note d90cd99169439d17f0152eff393f345c7ef8a1b5ea2fd71ee6d6eb62a43f0fa1. I read the complete assembled note and primary runner, checked all63 frozen files,46 runner inputs and41 recovery mappings, and reused previously reviewed parent identities. I authored several recovered implementation components and reviewed the constituent first-action/generator proofs; I did NOT author this canonical assembly. The independent contribution here is the assembled mathematical and scope check, not a newly claimed independent test of my own implementation.
+
+## Mathematical composition
+
+The family definition now makes the midpoint distinction explicit and correct: rational s and alpha define F itself; sqrt(alpha) conversion is outward for that exact family. A future action cannot switch to ideal Gauss roots while reusing its histories. Quadrature displacement remains separately allocated. Tuple(raw,Gamma-bit) coordinates and the explicit old399/new402 decoding avoid a silent covariance-index shift.
+
+All three q columns are necessary for the bare source span, not necessarily independent modulo F. Their self Gram, oriented negative center J, Ward-skew J and factor8 impurity action agree with the reviewed formulas. Original V remains in the798-column family;804 is only first-action DATA. DeltaK does not commute with Gamma, whereas free K does. Thus Gram rows in the correction are necessary on every Gamma input.
+
+The paired recurrence has the required positive Jc beta*j/r term because <Gamma b,seed>=−j. The normalized exact ideal coefficients form an isometry by the true projection recurrence, without asserting midpoint metric orthonormality. Shared physical history/Gram/scalar identity is indispensable and explicitly required. Outward interval dependence only widens enclosures; it does not justify favorable conditioning. Coefficient size/width gates are separate from the earlier forward coordinate certificate.
+
+The selected seed union and Gamma closure give R≤4k. Free action adds only Q; the impurity correction is in span{x0,qA} or{x0,qC}, including Gamma inputs. Thus U≤4k+8≤24 at k≤4, and principal M_U contains both C and its complete FIRST action. No second action, discarded coupling or large inverse is needed. For real coefficients T=CᵀMB is skew and compressed H=iT; hence leakage is BᵀMB+T². The note's Hermitian form G−A_V² is equivalent. Complex cases correctly use adjoints and Hermitian modulus. The row-sum enclosure bounds a PSD exact leakage matrix but does not imply it is small.
+
+The new-data trace and scalar sensitivity constants agree with the reviewed3d766 block. The old error is embedded once, new supported error added, complete804 arithmetic radius gated as a TOTAL. The corrected precise A contribution, rather than rounded2^41, is retained in the intermediate factor inequality. The stationary operator proximity budget is explicitly distinguished from action/C/leakage error; the imported geometry reserve remains a separate obligation.
+
+## Execution/recovery boundaries
+
+The frozen evidence shows five original four-pair PAIR_CAP outcomes. This is successful execution, not compression success. The DATA append count6015/2010 and extra closed trace5 are stated as bounded snapshots; the runner does not reconstruct native arrays or claim receipt existence proves physical interval containment. Twelve-pair continuation, actual C, DATA action, propagation and alpha remain excluded. Root/post archival limitations are disclosed rather than silently enlarged. Current flags are conditional-support/upstream_support, with no proposal or bare-retained permission and no claimed formal audit.
+
+The source pin recovery is consistent. Forty-one copied recovery items are preserved inputs, not imported executables in the portable runner. The95 reported checks comprise46 source-pin checks plus49 small mathematical predicates. The two recorded hash-rebound mutations fail the actual paired-sign and formal action-vector predicates, rather than merely triggering source-hash rejection. These are meaningful small controls, not physical solver mutations or infinite-model proofs. I did not rerun unchanged author controls or any native data.
+
+## Narrow wording correction
+
+The final supporting-controls paragraph says the runner checks a “dense tiny rank-two action.” Its actual code checks the norms and orthogonality of stipulated formal vectors b0=[1,−8,0] and b1=[0,0,1]; it does not construct and apply a dense K matrix. Replace this with “formal tiny rank-two action-vector identities” (or equivalent). The explanatory runner comment already accurately says formal orthonormal model. The mutation changing−8 to−4 remains a valid action-vector normalization control, with this scope. No proof or computational result changes.
+
+After this wording-only adjustment, an affected note/manifest check is sufficient. No physical replay or graph operation was performed for this review.
